{
  "comment": "The apps both sides build. One entry per app: the window it is shot at, the mode it is shot in, and the components it puts on screen. Both renderers read this, so neither has a list of its own. mode is content (the app builds a widget for the window's content area), window (the app builds its own toplevel, because a GtkWindow cannot be another window's content) or overlay (the app presents a dialog or popover over a host window, because those live above the content area rather than in it).",
